.TH PROF 1 2026-09-25 "Substrate" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
prof \- display profile data (not supported)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B prof
.RI [ argument ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B prof
is a stub.
Substrate has no
.I mon.out
or
.I gmon.out
profiling support, so there is never any profile data to display.
The command ignores all arguments, writes
.RS
.B prof: profiling is not supported on this system
.RE
to standard error, and exits with a failure status so that scripts can
detect the missing facility.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 1
Always.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cc (1),
.BR time (1)
